{%- comment -%} FAQ {%- endcomment -%}
<div class="agg-faq">
  <div class="agg-faq-inner">
    <div class="agg-faq-hdr">
      <span class="agg-sec-label">Common Questions</span>
      <div class="agg-sec-title">Frequently Asked Questions</div>
    </div>
    <div class="agg-faq-item open">
      <div class="agg-faq-q" onclick="aggToggleFaq(this)"><span class="agg-faq-q-text">Can I wear multiple gemstones at the same time?</span><span class="agg-faq-arrow">+</span></div>
      <div class="agg-faq-a"><p>Yes, but with caution. Certain planets are friendly to each other and their gemstones can be worn together. For example, Ruby (Sun), Red Coral (Mars) and Yellow Sapphire (Jupiter) are mutually friendly. However, some combinations like Ruby and Blue Sapphire (Sun and Saturn) are conflicting and should never be worn together. Always consult your astrologer.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="agg-faq-item">
      <div class="agg-faq-q" onclick="aggToggleFaq(this)"><span class="agg-faq-q-text">How long does it take for a gemstone to show effects?</span><span class="agg-faq-arrow">+</span></div>
      <div class="agg-faq-a"><p>Most wearers notice subtle changes within 7–30 days. Full effects typically manifest within 40–90 days. However, this depends on the quality of the stone, the strength of the planet in your chart and how consistently you wear it.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="agg-faq-item">
      <div class="agg-faq-q" onclick="aggToggleFaq(this)"><span class="agg-faq-q-text">What is the difference between natural and synthetic gemstones?</span><span class="agg-faq-arrow">+</span></div>
      <div class="agg-faq-a"><p>Natural gemstones form over millions of years under the earth's surface and carry the authentic vibrational energy used in Vedic astrology. Synthetic or lab-created stones may look identical but have no astrological benefit. Always insist on a certificate from a gemological laboratory confirming the stone is natural and untreated.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="agg-faq-item">
      <div class="agg-faq-q" onclick="aggToggleFaq(this)"><span class="agg-faq-q-text">What ratti (carat) weight should I choose?</span><span class="agg-faq-arrow">+</span></div>
      <div class="agg-faq-a"><p>The general guideline is 1 ratti per 10 kg of body weight, with a minimum of 2–3 ratti. However, the exact recommendation depends on your chart and the specific planet. Your astrologer will give you a precise recommendation based on your Kundali analysis.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="agg-faq-item">
      <div class="agg-faq-q" onclick="aggToggleFaq(this)"><span class="agg-faq-q-text">Can women wear the same gemstones as men?</span><span class="agg-faq-arrow">+</span></div>
      <div class="agg-faq-a"><p>Yes, the same gemstones apply to both men and women. The planet recommendations are based on the individual birth chart, not gender. The only difference is that women typically wear on the left hand and men on the right, based on traditional Vedic guidelines.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

